A||||8||FieroLisa||Idiot Mechanics...||||1||
Z||000000||FieroLisa||11-22-2000||09:38 PM||||Is it me, or do mechanics treat women like crap? <BR>I took my daily driver '94 Mercury Tracer to AATCO in Columbus 2 weeks ago. They promised to have the car done in 3-5 days so I gave them a credit card number.<BR>I go away for the weekend and when I get back, I call and they say "Bad news, this will run you $1300 for this and this and this" I said, fine, just get it done, I NEED it by Thanksgiving weekend.<BR>It was supposed to be done last Friday. I call, they say Monday, Tuesday I call and they say they are finishing it up as we speak. Today being Wednesday I decided to run up there and pick up my car. <BR>So I drive there, one of the mechanics came out and said "It's not done, It's a 'no-go'" I about went off on him..."You promised it in 5 days, that was over a 2 weeks ago, I need a car today, what am I supposed to do,and first and foremost why didn't you CALL me to tell me it's not done, etc" He then has the gall to say "Well, m'am, as soon as we diagnose it, we will know. I wanted to see if I could fix it first" So I told him "Well you obviously aren't diagnosing OR fixing much, since my car has been sitting in that parking lot for over 24 hours now. Not only that, the car started before, so this is obviously your fault!"<BR>Oh boy he was speechless. So who knows if the car will be done or not, they said "oh MAYbe by Monday..."<BR>But of course when I called him this evening, 6 hours later, he still hadn't started on it.<BR>AUGH. WHY. I'm so annoyed. <P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierospeeder||11-23-2000||04:28 AM||||I dont take my car to a mechanic ever, unless it would be tires, exhaust, or alignment.<P><BR>My mom brought her car to a mechanic, GM, and they broke stuff which wasn't broken.<BR>we kept on asking for the manager and he cut our price in half.<P>I would ask to speak to a manager.<P>Also, if they dont fix your car, you can go to small claims court and get another mechanic to fix it, and sue them for that amount plus what you already spent.<P>You can try calling your credit card company and try to get the charges removed and get your car towed away and brought to another mechanic.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||11-23-2000||05:18 AM||||Sounds like the same situation my wife dealt with a couple of times. When I first met her, she had taken her car in for a complete tune-up, belts, plugs wires, ball joints etc.,etc. About a week later one of the radiator hoses blew, then one of the beltrs twisted inside out, I looked at it and it was the wrong freakin belt, didn't even fit in the groove. She paid the guy like $1000 for all the work he supposedly did to her car.<BR>Another time I was away at basic training and she went to get two tires put on my car, I had bought two earlier for $70 each, the same garage charged her $100 each for the exact same tire. <P>Yes, mechanics do seem to mess with females more. I always try to explain stuff to my wife befor eshe even takes the car in so that she can go in there and act like she knows what she's talking about. Earns her a tiny bit more respect.<P>Jeff||||reg||1
Z||000003||hugh||11-23-2000||07:39 AM||||All business's are bottom line oriented,but some consider that to be the most important part of business and take advantage of their customers.You will probably not go back there,but someone who lives just around the corner from you will likely use the same garage,because they just don't know.You should file a complaint with the better business bureau.They can't really do anything,but anyone who may call asking about that place will be told there has been a problem,or multible problems if other people have complained.Good Luck!  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||11-23-2000||11:38 AM||||I would threaten them with legal action , They have had your car for such a long time , and they knew you needed it by a certian date...thus causing you to rent a car... Gimmie their phone # , let me chat with them , there is no reason that you should have to put up with PAYING for a rental car.. it's their fault , they promised a certian date....verbal contract....<P><BR>Don't take that kinda sh** ..<P>you better be here monday or else!!!!!! Lotsa snow here for you..<P>haha<P>Jonathan McCreery||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnnyK||11-23-2000||03:57 PM||||I am pretty sure I am going to complain to the BBB about Canadian Tire... They ALWAYS try to do uneccessary work. I went there to get pads changed.. Just the rear pads, cause I needed it for a trip to Kick Hill the next day. Go there, and they said "We'll do our free brake inspection".. I'm like, Ok, why not. Comes back, and says "YOu need new pads, rotors, calipers serviced, brake system flushed, and we'll put some new tires on" (Pretty sure the rotors were almost brand new, too). I'm like, NO, just the pads.. "We can't do that".. What the hell do you mean?? "We have to do it all. Otherwise, we could have the vehicle sit here and claim it Unsafe".. Bullsh*t. I just took it, and gave it to my real mechanic, who said, fine... Your tires look a little bald... Thats what I like.. God I'm mad now..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroLisa||11-23-2000||04:56 PM||||Legal Action is a pain in my @ss. I'm going through a case right now that's almost more work than its worth. (note I said almost).<P>I definitely need to find a mechanic I can trust- I have added a second to the list who have completely screwed me over. Fun. It would all be fine and good if anyone I knew and trusted could do tranny work, but that's what's been wrong both times with bad mechanics. <BR> <P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tigger||11-23-2000||05:42 PM||||I think it sucks...<P>Just the other day the lady that does my hair said the alternator in her (I think '97) Sunfire went out.  She said the bill was like $400!  I wanted to tell her it should have been only about an 1 hr or so labor and no more than $75 for parts, but she seemed pissed enough, and I think she knew she had been taken by the Pontiac dealer.<P>I agree with 2xsess, the best thing, if possible, is to have a friend check your car out first.||||reg||1
Z||000008||ChadMan||11-23-2000||08:35 PM||||Hey Lisa, if you're in Columbus right now, you might want to try my mechanic in Dublin, OH.  He does good work, he doesn't charge an exhorbitant markup on parts, and most importantly, he's honest.  Plus he knows his way around a Fiero.  On the down side, he doesn't take credit cards and he has been known to take an extra day or two to get your car back to you.  I'd rather wait an extra day or two for my car than have some f**kstick service manager try to charge me for a bunch of crap I don't need, or try to mark up parts by 100%.<P>If you're interested, email me at cmankins@copper.net and I'll give you his name and phone #. ||||reg||3
